  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>lscov</keyword>
  <short_description>Least-squares solution with known covariance.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>x = lscov(A, b)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>x = lscov(A, b, w)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>x = lscov(A, b, V)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>x = lscov(A, b, V, alg)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[x, stdx, mse, S] = lscov(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>A</param_name>
      <param_description>an m-by-n single or double matrix.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>b</param_name>
      <param_description>a single or double matrix with m rows.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>w</param_name>
      <param_description>a vector of m nonnegative weights.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>V</param_name>
      <param_description>an m-by-m symmetric positive semidefinite covariance matrix.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>alg</param_name>
      <param_description><b>'chol'</b> (default) or <b>'orth'</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>x</param_name>
      <param_description>the least-squares solution.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>stdx</param_name>
      <param_description>estimated standard errors of <b>x</b>.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>mse</param_name>
      <param_description>mean squared error of the weighted residuals.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>S</param_name>
      <param_description>estimated covariance matrix of <b>x</b> (single column <b>b</b> only).</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>x = lscov(A, b)</b> returns the ordinary least-squares solution of <b>A * x = b</b>.</p>
    <p><b>x = lscov(A, b, w)</b> minimizes <b>sum(w .* (b - A*x).^2)</b>. <b>x = lscov(A, b, V)</b> minimizes <b>(b - A*x)' * inv(V) * (b - A*x)</b>. When <b>V</b> is singular, the observations with zero variance are fitted exactly.</p>
    <p><b>mse</b> is the sum of squared weighted residuals divided by the degrees of freedom <b>m - rank(A)</b>, or 0 when there are none. <b>stdx</b> and <b>S</b> are scaled by <b>mse</b>.</p>
    <p>When <b>A</b> is rank deficient, a warning is shown and dependent coefficients are set to zero. <b>alg</b> is accepted for compatibility: both values use the same factorization.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
